          "en": "Supreme People's Procuratorate of the People's Republic of China\nANNOUNCEMENT\nThe Interpretation on Whether Knowledge Is Required Subjectively for the Constitution of the Crime of Paying for Sex with a Girl Under 14 was adopted at the 89th meeting of the Ninth Procuratorial Committee of the Supreme People's Procuratorate on 4 June 2001, and is hereby promulgated and shall come into force on 11 June 2001.\nSupreme People's Procuratorate\n11 June 2001\nInterpretation on Whether Knowledge Is Required Subjectively for the Constitution of the Crime\nof Paying for Sex with a Girl Under 14\n(Adopted at the 89th meeting of the Ninth Procuratorial Committee\nof the Supreme People's Procuratorate on 4 June 2001)\nGao Jian Fa Shi Zi No. 3 [2001]\nIn order to handle criminal cases of paying for sex with girls under 14 in accordance with law, the issues concerning the application of law to the act of paying for sex with a girl under 14 are interpreted as follows:\nWhere a person knows that the victim is or may be a girl under 14 and pays for sex with her, the provisions of paragraph 2 of Article 360 of the Criminal Law shall apply, and he shall be investigated for criminal responsibility for the crime of paying for sex with a girl under 14."
