          "en": "Supreme People's Procuratorate of the People's Republic of China\nAnnouncement\nThe Reply of the Supreme People's Procuratorate on How to Characterise the Act of Finding Another Person's Bank Card and Using It at an Automated Teller Machine (ATM) was adopted at the 92nd meeting of the Tenth Procuratorial Committee of the Supreme People's Procuratorate on 19 February 2008, is hereby promulgated, and shall come into force on 7 May 2008.\nSupreme People's Procuratorate\n18 April 2008\nSupreme People's Procuratorate\nReply on How to Characterise the Act of Finding Another Person's Bank Card and Using It at an Automated Teller Machine (ATM)\n(Adopted at the 92nd meeting of the Tenth Procuratorial Committee\nof the Supreme People's Procuratorate on 19 February 2008)\nGao Jian Fa Shi Zi No. 1 [2008]\nZhejiang Provincial People's Procuratorate:\nYour Procuratorate's Request for Instructions on How to Characterise the Act of Finding Another Person's Bank Card and Using It at an ATM (Zhe Jian Yan No. 227 [2007]) has been received. After study, the following reply is given:\nThe act of finding another person's bank card and using it at an automated teller machine (ATM) falls within the circumstance of \"fraudulently using another person's credit card\" as prescribed in subparagraph (c) of paragraph 1 of Article 196 of the Criminal Law; where the act constitutes a crime, criminal responsibility shall be investigated for the crime of credit card fraud.\nThis is our reply.\nSupreme People's Procuratorate\n18 April 2008"
